  "plain": "Test pilots of the secret U-2 and SR-71 spy planes were reportedly given gorilla masks, and told to put them on if they ever flew close enough to a civilian airliner for its pilot to see their faces. The philosopher Jason Jorjani tells Michels this from the journalist Annie Jacobsen's book Area 51. The point, as he tells it, is that the secret projects deliberately made sightings look absurd."
